# Python Backend Rules

- Target Python 3.11 or newer and add complete type hints to public functions.
- Keep domain modules independent of FastAPI, Pydantic, SQLite, and HTTP.
- Put orchestration in application services and external I/O behind injected
  collaborators.
- Use Pydantic models only at API and settings boundaries.
- Prefer immutable dataclasses for domain values and explicit return types.
- Never use live Monobank or NBU requests in automated tests.
- Map internal/upstream exceptions in the API adapter; domain code must not
  construct HTTP responses.
- Use Kyiv-aware dates and timestamps. Never use naive datetimes.
- Preserve money precision at contracts as decimal strings. Guard changes to
  current float calculations with parity fixtures.
- Keep synchronous blocking I/O outside async event-loop code.
- Log request metadata and outcomes, not tokens or transaction payloads.
- Run Ruff and pytest for touched Python code.
